      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Cale officially became an incorporated town on July 22, 1971, marking its formal recognition within Arkansas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://calearkansas.gov/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before the Civil War, federal land patents granted settlers such as Jessee C. and Capshaw, laying the groundwork for Cale's early farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        25,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cale_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After incorporation, Cale shifted from lumber to agriculture, cultivating cotton, corn, fruits, livestock, and poultry as its main economic drivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cale_arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Barham Lake, a reservoir on Cale's north end, offers two connected lakes separated by a road and a public park on the south shore.",
